rustc_target: the c33-unknown-linux-musl target

The C33 under no-MMU Linux with musl as a built-in target, so that a
standard library built for it can be installed in the sysroot and a
program built with --target c33-unknown-linux-musl, without -Zbuild-std
or a target spec file.  LLVM has no C33 back end: the target names gcc as
its default codegen backend, and carries the C33 GCC Linux driver's
defaults (-mcore=c33pe -mfdpic -msep-data) as llvm-args, which
rustc_codegen_gcc passes to libgccjit.

